6497e-07,-1.9073468138230965e-06,-4.0531076592742465e-06,-0.11134934425354004,-0.623515784740448,-4.291525328881107e-06,-0.0023913378827273846,-0.18529878556728363,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.00013243274588603526,-0.1754324585199356,0.0,-0.008265928365290165,-2.038458114839159e-05,-0.05512669309973717,-0.16269800066947937,-1.2097479104995728,0.0,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.000490068516228348,-2.7418097943154862e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,7824,315,279,444,324,352,356,33718,82,304,12989,6786,30161,1449,220,17,15,4420,13,8886,1899,304,5813,279,1156,7216,374,518,220,24,264,744,2572,323,279,1537,7216,8471,518,220,21,281,744,13,2585,1657,30161,525,1052,817,1899,304,5813,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe owners of the Luray Caverns in Virginia conduct tours every 20 minutes. Each day in April the first tour is at 9 a.m., and the last tour starts at 6 p.m. How many tours are there per day in April?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"4655308df82889783ae7e240eaa817f54ed6ccb2980d21adc8e78a5fa0bddb0f"},"seconds":25.00365400314331,"seed":719187531300007389,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of determining how many tours are conducted per day at the Luray Caverns in April, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the start and end times for tours**: The tours start at 9 a.m. and the last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n\n2. **Calculate the total time duration available for tours**: \n   - From 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. is 9 hours.\n   - Convert hours to minutes: \n     \\[\n     9 \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes/hour} = 540 \\text{ minutes}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Determine the frequency of tours**: Tours are given every 20 minutes.\n\n4. **Calculate the number of tours within the given time frame**: \n   - The total number of tours can be calculated by dividing the total available minutes by the duration between tours:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{540 \\text{ minutes}}{20 \\text{ minutes/tour}} = 27 \\text{ tours}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Verify the calculation**: \n   - Starting at 9:00 a.m., the first tour is at 9:00 a.m., and the tours continue every 20 minutes.\n   - The last tour should start at 6:00 p.m.:\n     \\[\n     9:00 \\text{ a.m.} + 26 \\times 20 \\text{ minutes} = 9:00 \\text{ a.m.} + 520 \\text{ minutes} = 6:00 \\text{ p.m.}\n     \\]\n   - This confirms that there are indeed 27 tours from 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m.\n\nThus, the number of tours per day in April is \\boxed{27}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{27}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
